      "instruction": "Follow docs/development-flow.md and docs/review-guidelines.md. Work only in your assigned worktree. Do not delegate or spawn subagents. Do not invoke live agent tests, push, publish, comment/review on GitHub or merge remote state; explicit GitWeave System Actions handle publication. Never redeem usage-limit reset tickets, buy allowance, or switch models/providers to bypass limits. Stop and return blocked if an actual permission/capability limitation prevents completion; do not invent an unsupported workaround or weaken requirements. Ordinary code/test defects are fixable findings, not capability blockers. Keep project material in English. Use deterministic tests and preserve existing behavior outside the issue's explicit change. Do not alter other worktrees or the original checkout.\n\nImplement Issue #24: simplify #17 to ordinary Git push/fetch of the selected Run's refs/gitweave/<run-id>/* and refs/notes/gitweave/<run-id>. Remove archive-specific abstractions/manifests, custom completeness/recovery/transaction protocols and unnecessary CLI surface. Preserve final Run records including final System Actions, attempt refs, notes, historical analysis from another checkout after merge/source deletion, unchanged artifact branches, and visible persistence failure. Use the smallest necessary destination selection compatible with existing workflows and local/offline Runs; explain the remaining rule in docs. Native Git commands can handle later fetch and retry; do not invent migration frameworks or stronger guarantees. Existing historical refs must remain inspectable through Git. Use focused local bare-remote integration tests, including recovery without original checkout and persistence failure, without live agents or live remote test data. Do not add protective policies without demonstrated need.\nImplement the whole supplied issue. Run all relevant deterministic checks. Leave final files for GitWeave to checkpoint. Return ready only after completion